  "raw_text": "Step 1: Calculate the area of the largest circle (radius 7).\nThe area of a circle is given by \\(A = \\pi r^2\\). For the largest circle, \\(r = 7\\), so the area is \\(\\pi \\times 7^2 = 49\\pi\\).\n\nStep 2: Calculate the area of the middle circle (radius 6).\nFor the middle circle, \\(r = 6\\), so the area is \\(\\pi \\times 6^2 = 36\\pi\\).\n\nStep 3: Calculate the area of the smallest circle (radius 4).\nFor the smallest circle, \\(r = 4\\), so the area is \\(\\pi \\times 4^2 = 16\\pi\\).\n\nStep 4: Determine the areas of regions X, Y, and Z.\n- Region X is the area of the largest circle minus the area of the middle circle, which is \\(49\\pi - 36\\pi = 13\\pi\\).\n- Region Y is the area of the middle circle minus the area of the smallest circle, which is \\(36\\pi - 16\\pi = 20\\pi\\).\n- Region Z is the area of the smallest circle, which is \\(16\\pi\\).\n\nStep 5: Identify the greatest and smallest areas among X, Y, and Z.\nThe greatest area is \\(20\\pi\\) (region Y) and the smallest area is \\(16\\pi\\) (region Z).\n\nStep 6: Calculate the difference between the greatest and smallest areas.\nThe difference is \\(20\\pi - 16\\pi = 4\\pi\\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{4\\pi}<|im_end|>",
  "reforward_peak_bytes": 15505560576,
  "script_sha256": "3d46237d3fa2d1d194ae8a3f4996120d3c1bf0d83b3c078c151f6660db552efa",
  "source": {
    "answer": "7\\pi",
    "level": 5,
    "problem": "In the diagram, the three concentric circles have radii of $4,$ $6,$ and $7.$ Three regions are labeled $X,$ $Y,$ or $Z$ below. Of these three regions, what is the difference between the area of the region with the greatest area and the area of the region with the smallest area? Express your answer in exact form.\n\n[asy]\nimport graph;\nfilldraw(circle((0,0),7), lightgray, black+linewidth(1));\nfilldraw(circle((0,0),6), gray, black+linewidth(1));\nfilldraw(circle((0,0),4), white, black+linewidth(1));\ndot((0,0));\nlabel(\"$X$\",(2,0));\nlabel(\"$Y$\",(5,0));\nlabel(\"$Z$\",(6.5,0));\n[/asy]",
    "solution": "The area of the inside circle (region $X$) is $\\pi\\cdot 4^2=16\\pi.$\n\nUsing a similar technique, the area of the middle ring (region $Y$) is $$\\pi\\cdot 6^2-\\pi\\cdot 4^2=36\\pi-16\\pi = 20\\pi.$$ Also, the area of the outer ring (region $Z$) is $$\\pi\\cdot 7^2-\\pi\\cdot 6^2=49\\pi - 36\\pi = 13\\pi.$$ Therefore, region $Y$ has the largest area and region $Z$ has the smallest area. The difference in their areas is $20\\pi-13\\pi = \\boxed{7\\pi}.$",
    "subject": "Prealgebra",
